<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr">
<head>
<%- include('partials/head') %>
</head>
<body>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>
<main>
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>How I got here</h1>

    <div class="about-layout">
      <aside class="reveal delay-0">
        <div class="facts-card">
          <div class="about-avatar">MD</div>
          <div class="fact">
            <span class="k">Based in</span>
            <span class="v">Tel Aviv District, Israel</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fact">
            <span class="k">Focus</span>
            <span class="v">Cloud infrastructure &amp; security</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fact">
            <span class="k">Currently</span>
            <span class="v status-live"><span class="dot"></span>Certified Network Defender &mdash; final stretch</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fact">
            <span class="k">Building</span>
            <span class="v">The AWS environment this site runs on</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>

      <div>
        <p class="lead reveal delay-1">
          I'm a hands-on operations and infrastructure professional with 5+
          years leading technical systems, cross-functional teams, and
          critical workflows across startup and nonprofit environments.
        </p>

        <p class="reveal delay-2">
          At XP.NETWORK, I helped launch and scale a multi-chain blockchain
          product, managing infrastructure across AWS, Cloudflare, MongoDB,
          and GitHub, coordinating investor communications, and supporting
          cross-team delivery from product to community. I also built the
          entire social and support ecosystem from scratch, including global
          moderator teams and platform integrations.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal delay-3">
          Outside of Web3, I've led major infrastructure projects for
          fundraising campaigns and nonprofits - overseeing real-time
          donation systems, registration platforms, payment integrations,
          DNS management, and stakeholder delivery on tight timelines.
        </p>

        <blockquote class="pull-quote reveal delay-4">
          I thrive where execution, clarity, and system thinking matter -
          bridging business needs with technical operations to move teams
          forward.
        </blockquote>

        <p class="reveal delay-5">
          That instinct is exactly what pulled me into cloud and security
          engineering directly. I'm in the final stretch of Bar-Ilan
          University's Certified Network Defender program - Active
          Directory/Azure, Check Point, Palo Alto, Cisco networking, Linux,
          and AWS architecture - and the capstone isn't a toy project. I
          designed and built a real multi-account AWS Organization: Entra
          ID SSO, a hub-and-spoke Transit Gateway network, encrypted
          multi-region storage, and a self-configured Palo Alto firewall
          bridged in over a genuine Site-to-Site VPN.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal delay-6">
          This site is deployed on that infrastructure. Not a demo of it -
          the actual thing.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
<%- include('partials/footer') %>
<script src="/static/js/reveal.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
